From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:47:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qosify: attach as tcx links, and learn DNS names on each
 device

qosify attached its classifiers as cls_bpf filters under clsact, and
redirected DNS replies to ifb-dns and the ingress to the interface's
ifb with tc filters: legacy filters on the WAN port beside einat's tcx
programs, which a qosify killed outright left behind. Its DNS learning
read the redirected packets as Ethernet frames, so that on pppoe-wan,
which has no link-layer header, it learnt nothing.

Carry two qosify patches. The first learns DNS names from a packet
socket on each device, without ifb-dns and its filters. The second
attaches the classifiers as tcx links after the programs there, has the
ingress classifier redirect to the ifb itself, and keeps cls_bpf under
clsact for kernels without tcx, or for the new defaults option tcx set
to 0, which the init script passes on. Both are meant for qosify
upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
